I will write a test that calls the method which contains the try-catch with the LogError call. From the snippet, it looks like the try-catch is inside a method that starts watchers on paths. I will find the method name and call it with a path that causes an exception to be thrown, so the catch block with LogError is hit.

I will submit a test file with a test class for LibraryMonitor, mocking dependencies and verifying that LogError is called on the ILogger when an exception occurs during watching a path.

