The test did not trigger the LogError call as expected. The exception might not be thrown because the FileSystemWatcher constructor might not throw for the invalid path string used or the code might swallow the exception differently.

I will try to trigger the exception by calling the public method ReportFileSystemChangeComplete with a path that causes an exception in the ReportFileSystemChanged method, which is called inside the try-catch with the LogError call.

I will also mock the ILibraryManager to throw an exception when ReportFileSystemChanged is called to simulate the error and verify the LogError call.

